-- Regression test for the DEEP PIN ruling (smucclaw/l4-ide#934).
--
-- `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (and its three sibling EVAL clause
-- builtins, and `VALUE AT`) used to restore the ambient temporal context the
-- moment the pinned expression reached WHNF. For a scalar that is exact
-- (WHNF = NF), but a constructor, record or list carries UNFORCED child
-- thunks out of the scope, and those were forced later, under the AMBIENT
-- context. The pin silently did not hold for them.
--
-- Pre-fix, case A below answered 7 (pinned, correct) while case B — the SAME
-- value, wrapped in a JUST — answered `JUST OF 9` (today's regime). Well
-- typed, no diagnostic, wrong law.
--
-- The pin is now DEEP: the pinned expression is forced to the same normal
-- form the evaluator prints, under the pin, before the context is restored.
--
-- Harness clock: JL4_FIXED_NOW = 2025-01-31T15:45:30Z, so the ambient
-- (unset-axis) rule date is 2025-01-31 — the NEW side of the 2024-01-01
-- changeover, hence 9.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

TIMEZONE IS "Etc/UTC"

DECLARE Assessment
    HAS rate    IS A NUMBER
        payable IS A NUMBER

-- GST rose from 7% to 9% for rules effective on/after 2024-01-01.
`GST rate` MEANS
    IF (DATE_SERIAL `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE`) AT LEAST (DATE_SERIAL (Date 1 1 2024))
    THEN 9
    ELSE 7

GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN Assessment
assess amount MEANS
    Assessment `GST rate` (amount TIMES `GST rate` DIVIDED BY 100)

GIVEN d IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE Assessment
`assess if given` d MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN JUST x  THEN JUST (assess x)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- A: scalar under the pin. WHNF = NF, so this was already right.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- expected: 7
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (Date 1 6 2023) `GST rate`

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- B-E: the same value behind one lazy constructor. Pre-fix all answered 9.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- expected: JUST OF 7
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (Date 1 6 2023) (JUST `GST rate`)

-- expected: LIST 7
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (Date 1 6 2023) (LIST `GST rate`)

-- expected: Assessment OF 7, 70
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (Date 1 6 2023) (assess 1000)

-- expected: JUST OF (Assessment OF 7, 70) — two constructors deep
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (Date 1 6 2023) (JUST (assess 1000))

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- F: the shape that was reported — the pin wraps a whole CONSIDER whose arm
-- builds a MAYBE. Pre-fix this needed the pin moved INSIDE the arm to work.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- expected: JUST OF (Assessment OF 7, 70)
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (Date 1 6 2023) (`assess if given` (JUST 1000))

-- expected: JUST OF (Assessment OF 9, 90) — the new regime, same expression
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (Date 1 7 2024) (`assess if given` (JUST 1000))

-- expected: NOTHING (no children to force; the pin is a no-op here)
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (Date 1 6 2023) (`assess if given` NOTHING)

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- G: the pin still RESTORES. Deep forcing must not leak the pinned context
-- outward, and a re-force under the old regime must flip back (the T6
-- WHNFWhen cache is revalidated per serve, not stale).
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- expected: JUST OF (Assessment OF 9, 90) — ambient
#EVAL `assess if given` (JUST 1000)

-- expected: JUST OF (Assessment OF 7, 70) — pinned again, after the ambient force
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (Date 1 6 2023) (`assess if given` (JUST 1000))

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- H: VALUE AT stamps the same axes per day and gets the same deep pin.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- expected: Assessment OF 7, 70
#EVAL `VALUE AT` (Date 1 6 2023) (GIVEN d YIELD assess 1000)

-- expected: Assessment OF 9, 90
#EVAL `VALUE AT` (Date 1 7 2024) (GIVEN d YIELD assess 1000)

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- I: THE REMAINING BOUNDARY, asserted deliberately.
--
-- A pin cannot follow a value into a scope it does not dominate. A CLOSURE
-- returned from under the pin is opaque to the deep force (as it is to the
-- printer): applying it later reads the AMBIENT context. This is the
-- documented limit of the ruling, not an oversight — see
-- specs/todo/TEMPORAL-RULE-VERSION-DESIGN.md §1.4.1.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

GIVETH A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER TO NUMBER
`rate plus` MEANS GIVEN n YIELD n PLUS `GST rate`

GIVEN f IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER TO NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`apply to zero` f MEANS f 0

-- expected: 9, NOT 7 — the closure escaped the pin unapplied.
#EVAL `apply to zero` (`EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (Date 1 6 2023) `rate plus`)

-- expected: 7 — applying it INSIDE the pin is the idiom that works.
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (Date 1 6 2023) (`apply to zero` `rate plus`)

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- J: THE SAME BOUNDARY, HIDDEN INSIDE DATA — and the fix makes it harder to
-- see, not easier.
--
-- Case I pins a bare closure, where the escape is at least legible at the pin
-- site: `EVAL UNDER … `rate plus`` visibly returns a function. Put the closure
-- in a record FIELD and the pin site returns a data value, with nothing in the
-- source to say one of its fields is still context-live.
--
-- Measured, `origin/unstable` @ 16adc022 vs this branch: PRE-fix the whole
-- pinned record read the ambient regime — rate 9 AND apply 900, wrong but
-- internally consistent. POST-fix the scalar field is pinned and the function
-- field is not, so ONE record answers 7 and 900 at the same time. No
-- diagnostic either way. See §1.4.1 "Closures".
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE Calc
    HAS rate  IS A NUMBER
        apply IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER TO NUMBER

GIVETH A Calc
calc MEANS Calc `GST rate` (GIVEN n YIELD n TIMES `GST rate`)

GIVEN f IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER TO NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`apply to hundred` f MEANS f 100

`pinned calc` MEANS `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (Date 1 6 2023) calc

-- expected: 7 — the scalar field IS pinned.
#EVAL `pinned calc`'s rate

-- expected: 900, NOT 700 — the function field of the SAME record is not.
#EVAL `apply to hundred` (`pinned calc`'s apply)

-- expected: 700 — applying inside the pin is the idiom that works.
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (Date 1 6 2023) (`apply to hundred` (calc's apply))

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- K: A REGULATIVE VALUE IS OPAQUE TO THE PIN, for the same structural reason
-- a closure is, and this is the boundary that matters most in practice
-- because the corpus's law-time axis is deontic.
--
-- `ValObligation`'s party and due are `Either RExpr (Value a)` and its
-- HENCE/LEST followups are bare `RExpr` closed over an `Environment`
-- (`jl4-core/src/L4/Evaluate/ValueLazy.hs`). `Foldable` on `Value` — which is
-- the deep pin's reachability relation, and `nfAux`'s — reaches none of them
-- in a freshly built obligation, so EVERY deadline is computed later by the
-- contract stepper under the AMBIENT context. The invariant "the pin covers
-- exactly what the evaluator prints" still holds; it just does not imply
-- coverage here, because what the printer prints for an obligation is the
-- deadline's unevaluated SOURCE (`WITHIN window`), not its value.
--
-- Byte-identical pre- and post-fix: not a regression, the edge of the ruling.
-- `window` is 30 under rules effective before 2024-01-01 and 10 on or after,
-- and the pinned trace below breaches at 10 — the ambient answer.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE Person IS ONE OF Alice, Bob
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF file, pay

window MEANS
    IF (DATE_SERIAL `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE`) AT LEAST (DATE_SERIAL (Date 1 1 2024))
    THEN 10
    ELSE 30

duty MEANS
  PARTY Alice
  MUST file
  WITHIN window
  HENCE (PARTY Bob MUST pay WITHIN window)

`pinned duty` MEANS `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (Date 1 6 2023) duty

-- expected: BREACHED at deadline 10 — the pinned window is 30, so a deep pin
-- would have this FULFILLED. The first obligation's own deadline escapes.
#TRACE `pinned duty` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES file AT 20

-- expected: BREACHED at deadline 11 — so does the HENCE continuation's.
#TRACE `pinned duty` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES file AT 1
  PARTY Bob DOES pay AT 20
